# Context snapshot (`.dump/`)

This repository uses **`.dump/`** at the **workspace root** for a **user-edited context snapshot**.

## Reading

- When the user asks to **reload context**, **continue where we left off**, **restore the snapshot**, or **@-references** a path under **`.dump/`**, read **only** the referenced file(s). Do **not** bulk-enumerate **`.dump/`** unless the user asks.
- Default handoff file: **`.dump/CONTEXT_SNAPSHOT.md`**. Dated checkpoints: **`.dump/YYYY-MM-DD-context.md`** (if present).
- Treat the snapshot as **hints**: verify against the codebase when something may be stale.

## Writing

- After substantive work, if the user wants continuity, **offer** to refresh **`.dump/CONTEXT_SNAPSHOT.md`** (or add a dated **`.dump/YYYY-MM-DD-context.md`**) using the template already in **`CONTEXT_SNAPSHOT.md`**.
- Keep snapshots **compact** (goal, decisions, files touched, open items, **one** next step). No secrets.

## Indexing

- **`.dump/`** is **not** listed in **`.cursorignore`** so **@-search** can find these files. If a snapshot ever contains sensitive material, split: public template here, private notes elsewhere (and/or **`.gitignore`**).

## Global rule

- Cross-project behavior is also described in **`~/z/env/ai/cursor/rules/chat-context-and-transcripts.mdc`** (section **Context snapshot**).
